map "Name" {(pair <key> <val>)\u2026})` fills a\n * named integer map read by `(mapEntry "Name" <key>)`. Tokens resolve\n * statically: numbers stay as-is\x2C `FirstSite`/`LastSite` point at the board's\n * store holes\x2C role idents (P1\u2026) become player ids\x2C and coordinate strings\n * ("D1") become site indices.\n */\nfunction compileMap(equipment\x2C env) {\n    const storeMap = env.playerStoreMap;\n    if (!storeMap)\n        return;\n    const stores = env.board.stores;\n    const { width } = env.board;\n    const resolveToken = (node) => {\n        if (isNumber(node))\n            return node.value;\n        if (isIdent(node)) {\n            if (node.name === "FirstSite")\n                return stores[0];\n            if (node.name === "LastSite")\n                return stores[stores.length - 1];\n            return playerOfRole(node.name);\n        }\n        if (isString(node)) {\n            const c = parseCoordToSite(node.value\x2C width);\n            if (c !== undefined)\n                return c;\n        }\n        return undefined;\n    };\n    const pairsOf = (mapNode) => {\n        const out = [];\n        const scan = (node) => {\n            for (const item of node.items) {\n                if (!isList(item))\n                    continue;\n                if (listHead(item) === "pair") {\n                    const k = item.items[1] ? resolveToken(item.items[1]) : undefined;\n                    const v = item.items[2] ? resolveToken(item.items[2]) : undefined;\n                    if (k !== undefined && v !== undefined)\n                        out.push([k\x2C v]);\n                }\n                else if (item.delimiter === "curly") {\n                    scan(item);\n                }\n            }\n        };\n        scan(mapNode);\n        return out;\n    };\n    const scanEquip = (node) => {\n        for (const item of node.items) {\n            if (!isList(item))\n                continue;\n            if (listHead(item) === "map") {\n                const nameNode = item.items[1];\n                const pairs = pairsOf(item);\n                if (nameNode && isString(nameNode)) {\n                    const named = new Map(pairs);\n                    env.namedMaps?.set(nameNode.value\x2C named);\n                }\n                else {\n                    for (const [k\x2C v] of pairs)\n                        storeMap.set(k\x2C v);\n                }\n            }\n            else if (item.delimiter === "curly") {\n                scanEquip(item);\n            }\n        }\n    };\n    scanEquip(equipment);\n}\n/** Parse a chess-style coordinate ("D1") to a 0-based site index on a board of\n * the given width (origin bottom-left)\x2C or undefined if not a coordinate. */\nfunction parseCoordToSite(s\x2C width) {\n    const m = /^([A-Za-z]+)(\\d+)$/.exec(s.trim());\n    if (!m?.[1] || !m[2])\n        return undefined;\n    let col = 0;\n    for (const ch of m[1].toUpperCase())\n        col = col * 26 + (ch.charCodeAt(0) - 64);\n    return (Number(m[2]) - 1) * width + (col - 1);\n}\n/**\n * Resolve a `(place "Label" \u2026)` label to its owning player. A direct hit on\n * the piece-owner map wins (covers `Each`-keyed pieces and exact labels). When\n * a piece is declared `(piece "Disc" P1)` the map is keyed by the bare label\x2C\n * but placements use the Ludii convention `"Disc1"` where the trailing digits\n * are the player index \u2014 so fall back to stripping that suffix.\n */\nfunction resolvePlacementOwner(label\x2C env) {\n    const direct = env.pieceOwner.get(label);\n    if (direct !== undefined)\n        return direct;\n    const m = /^(.*?)(\\d+)$/.exec(label);\n    if (m?.[1] !== undefined && m[2] !== undefined && env.pieceOwner.has(m[1])) {\n        return Number(m[2]);\n    }\n    return undefined;\n}\n/**\n * Resolve a `(place "Label" \u2026)` label to its component `what` id\x2C using the\n * same label/suffix scheme as {@link resolvePlacementOwner}. Returns undefined\n * when the label isn't a known component (placement then defaults `what` to the\n * owner\x2C preserving single-piece-per-player behaviour).\n */\nfunction resolvePlacementWhat(label\x2C env) {\n    const map = env.componentIdByLabel;\n    if (!map)\n        return undefined;\n    const direct = map.get(label);\n    if (direct !== undefined)\n        return direct;\n    // "Pawn1" \u2192 component "Pawn1" already covered; also handle a bare base label\n    // that was registered per-player (rare for placement\x2C but symmetric).\n    const m = /^(.*?)(\\d+)$/.exec(label);\n    if (m?.[1] !== undefined && m[2] !== undefined) {\n        const withSuffix = map.get(label);\n        if (withSuffix !== undefined)\n            return withSuffix;\n    }\n    return undefined;\n}\n/**\n * Resolve a `(place "Label" \u2026)` to every owning player it names. Unlike\n * {@link resolvePlacementOwner}\x2C a bare base label declared as an `Each` piece\n * (keyed `"Marker1"`\x2C `"Marker2"`\x2C \u2026 in the owner map) expands to ALL those\n * players \u2014 so `(place "Marker" "Hand")` seeds every player's hand.\n */\nfunction resolvePlacementOwners(label\x2C env) {\n    const direct = resolvePlacementOwner(label\x2C env);\n    if (direct !== undefined)\n        return [direct];\n    const owners = [];\n    for (let p = 1; p <= env.numPlayers; p += 1) {\n        const owner = env.pieceOwner.get(`${label}${p}`);\n        if (owner !== undefined)\n            owners.push(owner);\n    }\n    return owners;\n}\n/** Read a `name:<int>` argument from a ludeme's item list (e.g. `count:3`). */\nfunction readNamedInt(items\x2C name) {\n    const idx = items.findIndex((n) => isIdent(n) && n.name === `${name}:`);\n    if (idx < 0)\n        return undefined;\n    const v = items[idx + 1];\n    return v && isNumber(v) ? v.value : undefined;\n}\n/** Read a named curly int-list argument (e.g. `counts:{5 5 5 5}`). */\nfunction readNamedIntList(items\x2C name) {\n    const idx = items.findInde